1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,400
ENOCH: The year is completed in 364 days

2
00:00:04,811 --> 00:00:05,811
MAYA: Respectfully?

3
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:06,571
MAYA: No.

4
00:00:06,871 --> 00:00:10,011
MAYA: Earth takes 365.24 days

5
00:00:10,507 --> 00:00:12,187
ENOCH: A mere day and a quarter.

6
00:00:12,407 --> 00:00:13,647
ENOCH: What harm can it do?

7
00:00:13,951 --> 00:00:16,911
MAYA: Your calendar slips a day and a quarter every year.

8
00:00:17,311 --> 00:00:20,871
MAYA: In ten years, every feast lands twelve days early

9
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:27,400
MAYA: After 147 years Midsummer falls in the middle of winter

10
00:00:27,698 --> 00:00:30,098
ENOCH: Then let the earth obey the calendar

11
00:00:30,718 --> 00:00:33,918
MAYA: Okay, but that's the scary part

12
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:36,939
MAYA: To finish its orbit a day and a quarter sooner,

13
00:00:37,219 --> 00:00:39,239
MAYA: Earth has to move closer to the sun,

14
00:00:39,899 --> 00:00:45,659
MAYA: 339,000 kilometers closer, almost the distance to the moon

15
00:00:46,096 --> 00:00:47,176
ENOCH: And the sunlight?

16
00:00:47,654 --> 00:00:49,274
MAYA: Half a percent stronger.

17
00:00:49,654 --> 00:00:54,774
MAYA: That's about forty percent of all the warming push humans have added since 1750.

18
00:00:55,939 --> 00:00:58,279
ENOCH: So we fix the calendar?

19
00:00:58,865 --> 00:01:02,165
MAYA: Or we move the planet You decide

